### DPDMS demo requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client format)
### Run top to bottom for the full demo. Swagger-style docs: docs/03-API-REFERENCE.md

### 0. Login as the seeded admin (see auth-service README for the bootstrap SQL)
# @name admin
POST http://localhost:8888/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "admin", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

### Create the accounts for the demo (admin token required - paste from step 0)
POST http://localhost:8888/api/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "sean", "password": "Passw0rd!", "fullName": "T. Chirwa", "role": "WARD_RECORDER", "ward": "Mudzi", "hazard": "fire"}

###

POST http://localhost:8888/api/auth/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "oliver", "password": "Passw0rd!", "fullName": "Mrs Moyo", "role": "PROVINCIAL_SUPERVISOR", "hazard": "fire"}

### 1. Login as the fire recorder
# @name recorder
POST http://localhost:8888/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "sean", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

### 2. Recorder captures a fire incident (status comes back PENDING)
# @name created
POST http://localhost:8888/api/fires
Authorization: Bearer {{recorder.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ward": "Mudzi", "district": "Mudzi", "province": "Mashonaland Central",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-20T14:30:00", "reporter": "T. Chirwa",
  "severity": "HIGH", "latitude": -17.4, "longitude": 31.6,
  "areaBurnedHectares": 45.5, "suspectedCause": "Land clearing fire that spread",
  "injuries": 1, "fatalities": 0, "structuresDestroyed": 2, "fireStatus": "ACTIVE"
}

### 3. Try to approve as the RECORDER -> must be 403 (recorders cannot review)
PATCH http://localhost:8888/api/fires/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{recorder.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. Login as the fire supervisor
# @name supervisor
POST http://localhost:8888/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "oliver", "password": "Passw0rd!"}

### 5. Supervisor approves -> audit fields set + alert-service notified
PATCH http://localhost:8888/api/fires/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.token}}

### 6. Try to EDIT the approved record -> 403 (approved records are locked)
PUT http://localhost:8888/api/fires/{{created.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{recorder.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ward": "Mudzi", "district": "Mudzi", "province": "Mashonaland Central",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-20T15:00:00", "reporter": "T. Chirwa",
  "severity": "CRITICAL", "latitude": -17.4, "longitude": 31.6,
  "areaBurnedHectares": 60, "suspectedCause": "Updated cause",
  "injuries": 2, "fatalities": 0, "structuresDestroyed": 3, "fireStatus": "CONTAINED"
}

### 7. Supervisor requests corrections on a second incident (create one first)
POST http://localhost:8888/api/fires
Authorization: Bearer {{recorder.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ward": "Mudzi", "district": "Mudzi", "province": "Mashonaland Central",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-22T11:00:00", "reporter": "T. Chirwa",
  "severity": "MEDIUM", "latitude": -17.2, "longitude": 31.7,
  "areaBurnedHectares": 8, "suspectedCause": "Bee smoking",
  "injuries": 0, "fatalities": 0, "structuresDestroyed": 0, "fireStatus": "CONTAINED"
}

###

PATCH http://localhost:8888/api/fires/2/request-corrections
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"notes": "Confirm the area burned with the forestry office"}

### 8. Approved-only feed (what reports, dashboard and alerts consume)
GET http://localhost:8888/api/fires

### 9. Reports in four formats (Rejoice's report-service)
GET http://localhost:8888/api/reports/fires?format=pdf

###

GET http://localhost:8888/api/reports/fires?format=xlsx
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisor.response.body.$.token}}

### 10. Alert log (Todzani's alert-service - see the approval produced rows)
GET http://localhost:8888/api/alerts

### 11. Pull approved incidents from ALL five hazards and alert new ones
POST http://localhost:8888/api/alerts/scan

### 12. Dashboard summary (Oliver's dashboard-service)
GET http://localhost:8888/api/dashboard/summary

### 13. Health check per hazard service
GET http://localhost:8888/api/dashboard/health
